# SOLID Principles (Pragmatic & Lean)

Apply SOLID to **real code**, not as an excuse for premature indirection. Full reference: `docs/ARCHITECTURE_CODING_STANDARDS.md`.

## Single Responsibility (S)
- Routes define HTTP methods and paths; controllers handle validation and response transformation; services/lib contain business logic (e.g. `haversine.ts`); Prisma handles database persistence.
- React components render UI; custom hooks fetch and manage state; `src/lib/api.ts` performs typed API requests.

## Open/Closed (O)
- Extend functionality through function composition and pure functions rather than complex inheritance hierarchies.

## Liskov Substitution (L)
- Test fakes, SQLite test databases, and production Neon PostgreSQL clients must honor the identical Prisma query contracts and transactional guarantees.

## Interface Segregation (I)
- Keep DTOs and type definitions lean. Don't bundle internal admin-only audit fields into public explorer vendor types.

## Dependency Inversion (D)
- Decouple controllers from raw DB sockets by consuming Prisma through the initialized client in `src/lib/prisma.ts`.
